  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1129 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nThunderstorms will likely be ongoing Friday evening, with a\ngradual shift south and eastward through the overnight. As noted\nyesterday, potential for some low shower and thunderstorm chances\nto hang on in parts of the area during the day Saturday is now\ndepicted in the NBM data, largely focused across parts of\nsoutheast Oklahoma into west central Arkansas. While the POPs from\nthe NBM have been adjusted slightly to more uniformly depict the\nthreat, their message is largely maintained. To the north of this\npotential activity on Saturday, temperatures will reach the triple\ndigits across a widespread area once again, with heat headlines \nagain possible across a larger part of northeast Oklahoma. With\nthe upper level ridge expanding eastward across the region to\nclose out the weekend and continue through much of the week ahead,\ndry and hot conditions will prevail once again through at least\nthe middle of the week. There are signs that the ridge shifts\nsouthward some for the latter part of the week, with potential for\nanother round of showers and thunderstorms and cooler\ntemperatures.",
